<% layout('/layouts/base') %>

<div class="page-header">
  <h1>Chrome extension</h1>
</div>

<section class="form-card stack">
  <p>
    The Carton Cache extension adds a side panel to Chrome for finding the right carton
    from your inventory while you list and ship, without leaving the page you're on.
  </p>

  <a href="/extension/download" class="btn btn--primary" download>Download extension (v<%= it.version %>)</a>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <ol class="stack">
    <li>Unzip the downloaded file. Keep the <code>carton-cache-extension</code> folder somewhere permanent, since Chrome loads the extension from it.</li>
    <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> in Chrome.</li>
    <li>Turn on <strong>Developer mode</strong> (top right).</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Load unpacked</strong> and select the <code>carton-cache-extension</code> folder.</li>
    <li>Click the Carton Cache icon in the toolbar to open the side panel, enter <code><%= it.origin %></code> as the Carton Cache URL, and log in when asked.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Update</h2>
  <p>
    The extension doesn't update itself. To update, download it again, replace the contents of the
    <code>carton-cache-extension</code> folder, and click the reload icon on the extension's card in
    <code>chrome://extensions</code>.
  </p>
</section>
